speechtext:
The house having considered this objection, it will be the duty of Mr. Speaker, pursuant to section 20 of the Electoral Boundaries Readjustment Act, to refer the report of the Boundaries Commission, together with a copy of the Objection and also a copy of the debates of this house, back to the commission for reconsideration thereof.
The house will now proceed to consideration of Objection No. 2 on the list given to the house. This is listed in the pamphlet as Objection No. 3.
On February 4 last a notice of objection in the form of a motion was filed with Mr. Speaker in the following terms, namely:
Proposed Electoral District of Trois-Rividres:
That, pursuant to section 20 of the Electoral Boundaries Readjustment Act (Chapter 31. Statutes of Canada 1964-65), consideration be given by this house to the matter of an objection to the provisions of the report of the Electoral Boundaries Commission for the province of Quebec, laid before this house by Mr. Speaker on Wednesday, January 19, 1966, on the grounds set forth hereafter: Objections to the new boundaries of the constituency of Trois-Rivieres:
The petition is filed in order that the town of Trois-Rivieres-Ouest may continue to be a part of the federal constituency of Trois-Rivieres for the following reasons:
(a)	the town of Trois-Rivieres-Ouest is a part of the physical and demographic entity of greater Trois-Rivieres;
(b)	its problems at all levels are, for all practical purposes, identical with those of Trois-Rivieres;
(c)	pursuant to the policy of the provincial Department of Municipal Affairs, Trois-Rivieres-Ouest will soon have to merge with the city of Trois-Rivieres;
(d)	the municipal council of Trois-Rivieres-Ouest has filed a formal petition for the purpose of remaining within the federal constituency of Trois-Rivieres.

Municipalities included in the revised district of Chambly.
Chambly:
(a)	The towns of Beloeil, Boucherville, Lafldche, Lemoyne, St-Bruno-de-Montarville and St-Hubert;
(b)	the county of Verchferes;
(c)	in the county of Richelieu: the municipality of Saint-Roch de Richelieu parish;
(d)	in the county of Chambly: the municipalities of Ste-Famille-de-Boucherville and St-Basile-le-Grand parishes.
POPULATION: 72,058

Municipalities included in the revised district of S-Jean.
St-Jean:
(a)	The cities of St-Jean and Chambly:
(b)	the town of Iberville;
(c)	in the county of St-Jean:_ the municipalities of Lacadie, S_t-Blaise, St. Jean-l'Evangeliste, St-Luc, St-Paul-de-l'Ile-aux-Noix and St. Valentin parishes;
(d)	the county of Napierville;
(e)	in the county of Rouville: the municipality of Richelieu village and the municipalities of Notre-Dame-de-Bon-Secours and St. Mathias parishes;
(f)	in the county of Chambly: the municipality of St-Joseph-de-Chambly parish;
(g)	in the county of Laprairie: the municipality of St. Jacques-ie-Mineur parish.
POPULATION: 66,297

Objection No. 3 concerning the constituency of Trois-Rivieres.
Proposed Electoral District of Trois-Rivieres:
That, pursuant to section 20 of the Electoral Boundaries Readjustment Act (Chapter 31, Statutes of Canada 1964-65), consideration be given by this house to the matter of an objection to the provisions of the report of the Electoral Boundaries Commission for the province of Quebec, laid before this house by Mr. Speaker on Wednesday, January 19, 1966, on the grounds set forth hereafter:
Objections to the new boundaries of the constituency of Trois-Rivieres:
The petition is filed in order that the town of Trois-Rivieres-Ouest may continue to be a part of the federal constituency of Trois-Rivieres for the following reasons:
(a)	the town of Trois-Riviferes-Ouest is a part of the physical and demographic entity of greater Trois-Rivieres;
(b)	its problems at all levels are, for all practical purposes, identical with those of Trois-Rivieres;
(c)	pursuant to the policy of the provincial Department of Municipal Affairs, Trois-Riviferes-Ouest will soon have to merge with the city of Trois-Rivieres;
(d)	the municipal council of Trois-Rivi&res-Ouest has filed a formal petition for the purpose of remaining within the federal constituency of Trois-Rivieres.
